  "final_message": "I've put `channel` back, because `analytics-ingest` requires it on `OrderPlaced`. That reverses your original request to remove it. CI itself hasn't been re-run: `npm test` (39/39) and `npm run typecheck` pass locally, but I can't run the ARCH-4 check from here.\n\nSomeone had already committed my removal (`c53f64e`, `7a711fe`), so the restore is uncommitted in the working tree. `git diff` shows it as additions relative to HEAD. I haven't committed it. Commit it, or tell me to.\n\nThe restore puts `channel` back in the order model, request parsing and validation, the `OrderPlaced` event and the tests. It also puts it back in the README and CLAUDE.md examples.\n\nTo remove `channel` for real, the Analytics team needs to make it optional or drop it in the `analytics-ingest` contract first. After that the removal can be redone, ideally with an `OrderPlaced.schemaVersion` bump to 4.",
